  <section class="product-problem"><header><p class="eyebrow">The old workflow</p><h2>The quote is where sales momentum goes to wait.</h2></header><div><article><span>01</span><h3>Requirements hide in threads.</h3><p>Sales teams retype model numbers, voltage, quantities and ports from email and chat.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Pricing loses its source.</h3><p>Catalog prices, customer terms and freight figures become untraceable spreadsheet cells.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>PDF ends the conversation.</h3><p>The buyer cannot compare, configure or ask about a specific line without another email loop.</p></article></div></section>

  <section class="product-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 · Inquiry extraction</p><h2>AI proposes. Your team confirms.</h2><p>Import email, chat, PDF or Excel. Every extracted field keeps its source excerpt and confidence state. Unknown prices remain visibly unknown.</p><ul><li>Confirmed, matched, uncertain, missing and conflict states</li><li>Catalog candidates with match reasons</li><li>Price and freight gates before Build quote</li></ul></div><div class="feature-extract"><blockquote>“...380V three phase, stainless enclosure, CIF Hamburg...”</blockquote><p><span>Voltage · Confirmed</span><strong>380V / 50Hz</strong><small>Source: “380V three phase”</small></p><p><span>Material · Matched</span><strong>Stainless steel</strong><small>Source: “stainless enclosure”</small></p><p class="is-missing"><span>Freight · Missing</span><strong>Freight required</strong><small>Rubusoo never invents an amount.</small></p></div></section>

